## Summary

The repository is a Spring/OfficeFloor PetClinic variant. All owner-creation business rules are implemented as small single-method "function" classes wired together by a YAML pipeline. Duplicate detection is centered on a derived `identityKey`.

Important finding up front: there is a mismatch between the current implementation and what the tests/docstrings call "identity-key-v2". The current `identityKey` is a plaintext pipe-delimited string with no hashing and no soundex, but `AcceptanceTest` expects a 64-char lowercase SHA-256 hex string built over `soundex(lastName)`. No soundex implementation exists anywhere in the repo. Details below.

---

## 1. Files involved in computing the owner identity key

- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java` — defines `getIdentityKey()` and the `householdId`, `telephone`, `email`, `possibleDuplicateOf`, `deleted` fields.
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/EnsureUniqueIdentity.java` — the 409 duplicate check keyed on `identityKey`.
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AssignHouseholdId.java` — stamps `householdId` (part of the key).
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/Household.java` — household id derivation + last-name normalization.
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Sha256.java` — SHA-256 hex utility (used by household id + customer code, NOT by identityKey today).
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/NormalizeOwnerTelephone.java` + `E164Telephone.java` + `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/E164.java` — telephone normalization (part of key).
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/NormalizeOwnerEmail.java` — email lowercasing (part of key).
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` — the create-owner pipeline ordering.
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml` (lines ~2284-2312) — API schema/description of `identityKey`, `possibleDuplicate`, `possibleDuplicateOf`, `householdId`, and the request-only `sharesHousehold` (line 2097).
- Tests: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java` and `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java`.

---

## 2. Current identity-key formula

`Owner.java` lines 361-374:

```java
@Transient
public String getIdentityKey() {
    return blankToEmpty(this.telephone) + '|' + blankToEmpty(this.email) + '|' + blankToEmpty(this.householdId);
}
private static String blankToEmpty(String value) {
    return (value == null) ? "" : value;
}
```

So today the key is the plaintext `"<telephone>|<email>|<householdId>"` (each empty-string when null). It is NOT hashed and does NOT use last name or soundex. The `householdId` component itself is a 12-char SHA-256 prefix (see section 5).

Note the divergence: `AcceptanceTest.java` (lines 9-19) documents "identity-key-v2 = SHA-256 hex over (normalizedTelephone | lowerEmail | soundex(lastName))" and asserts `key.matches("[0-9a-f]{64}")`. The current implementation would fail that assertion (it returns plaintext with `|` separators and a hex-uppercase household segment). This is the redesign target.

---

## 3. Duplicate detection (409 Conflict path)

`EnsureUniqueIdentity.java` lines 20-30:

```java
public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) throws DuplicateIdentityException {
    String identityKey = owner.getIdentityKey();
    for (Owner existing : ownerRepository.findByTelephone(owner.getTelephone())) {
        if (!existing.isDeleted() && identityKey.equals(existing.getIdentityKey())) {
            throw new DuplicateIdentityException(identityKey);
        }
    }
}
```

- Candidate set is narrowed via `ownerRepository.findByTelephone(owner.getTelephone())` (repository method declared at `/home/daniel/sandbox/.../repository/OwnerRepository.java:68`). This works only because telephone is a component of the key.
- Deleted owners are ignored via `!existing.isDeleted()`.
- On a full-key match it throws `DuplicateIdentityException`.

Exception + handler:
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/DuplicateIdentityException.java` — message `"Identity key is already in use: " + identityKey`.
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/DuplicateIdentityExceptionHandler.java` lines 13-16 responds `HttpStatus.CONFLICT` (409) with body `{"errors":["identityKey"]}`.
- Wired by `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/escalation/org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.DuplicateIdentityException.yml`.

Email-domain blocklist — this is a SEPARATE step (400, not part of the 409 path), in `RejectDisposableEmail.java`:

```java
private static final Set<String> DISPOSABLE_DOMAINS = Set.of(
        "mailinator.com", "tempmail.com", "guerrillamail.com");
...
String domain = email.substring(email.indexOf('@') + 1).toLowerCase();
if (DISPOSABLE_DOMAINS.contains(domain)) {
    throw new DisposableEmailException(domain);
}
```

It runs in the pipeline right after email normalization and before `BuildOwner` (owners.POST.yml lines 44-46), so it is not inside the identity/409 logic. The blocklist is a hardcoded 3-domain `Set`. Exception class: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/DisposableEmailException.java` (maps to 400 elsewhere).

---

## 4. Soft-match logic

`DetectPossibleDuplicate.java` lines 22-42:

```java
public void service(@Val Owner owner, @Val DeclaredHouseholdMember declaredMember,
        OwnerRepository ownerRepository) {
    if (declaredMember != null) {
        return;
    }
    String householdId = owner.getHouseholdId();
    if (householdId == null || householdId.isBlank()) {
        return;
    }
    ownerRepository.findByLastName(owner.getLastName()).stream()
        .filter(existing -> householdId.equals(existing.getHouseholdId())
            && existing.getTelephone() != null
            && !existing.getTelephone().equals(owner.getTelephone()))
        .map(Owner::getId)
        .filter(id -> id != null)
        .min(Integer::compareTo)
        .ifPresent(owner::setPossibleDuplicateOf);
}
```

Trigger conditions:
- Skipped entirely if the owner is a declared household member (see section 5).
- Skipped if the owner has no `householdId` (i.e. no postcode).
- Otherwise, among owners with the same last name, it finds existing owners with the SAME `householdId` but a DIFFERENT (non-null) telephone, takes the lowest such id, and records it via `owner.setPossibleDuplicateOf(...)`.
- Note: this filter does NOT exclude deleted owners (unlike the 409 path).
- The `possibleDuplicate` boolean is derived in `Owner.getPossibleDuplicate()` (lines 267-270) as `possibleDuplicateOf != null`.

Runs after `EnsureUniqueIdentity` and just before `SaveOwner` (owners.POST.yml lines 108-111), so the flag persists.

`DeclaredHouseholdMember` marker enum: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/DeclaredHouseholdMember.java`.

---

## 5. HouseholdId computation and household-duplicate 409 block

Household id — `Household.java` lines 28-44:

```java
static String normalizeLastName(String lastName) {
    return lastName == null ? "" : lastName.strip().replaceAll("\\s+", " ").toLowerCase(Locale.ROOT);
}
...
static String idFor(String lastName, String postcode) {
    if (!StringUtils.hasText(postcode)) {
        return null;
    }
    return Sha256.hex(normalizeLastName(lastName) + '|' + postcode).substring(0, ID_LENGTH);
}
```

- `ID_LENGTH = 12` (line 23). So `householdId` = first 12 chars of uppercase-hex `SHA-256(normalizedLastName + "|" + postcode)`.
- `normalizeLastName`: strip, collapse inner whitespace to single spaces, lowercase (ROOT locale).
- Returns null when no postcode (owner belongs to no household).
- Stamped by `AssignHouseholdId.service()` (line 18-20).
- `Household.existingMembers(owner, repo)` (lines 51-59) returns persisted owners sharing the same `householdId` (does not filter deleted here).

Household-duplicate 409 block: There is no longer a separate household-duplicate check. It has been folded into `EnsureUniqueIdentity` because `householdId` is a component of `identityKey` (documented in the class Javadoc of `EnsureUniqueIdentity.java` lines 9-18 and `DuplicateIdentityException.java`). Two same-household owners with different telephones get different keys and are both allowed; only an exact full-key match is a 409.

Declared-member handling — `MarkDeclaredHouseholdMember.java` lines 23-36:

```java
public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request, @Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository,
        Out<DeclaredHouseholdMember> declaredMember) {
    if (!Boolean.TRUE.equals(request.getSharesHousehold())) {
        return;
    }
    boolean occupied = Household.existingMembers(owner, ownerRepository).stream()
            .anyMatch(existing -> !existing.isDeleted());
    if (occupied) {
        declaredMember.set(DeclaredHouseholdMember.INSTANCE);
    }
